#: ../../../reference/metadata.rst:73
msgid ""
"Arguments forwarded to the backend at install time, replayed by later "
"``upgrade`` and ``reinstall`` runs. pipx reads them as `pip <https://"
"pip.pypa.io>`_ does and stores each option under its full name, so it stores "
"a clustered ``-qf wheels`` as ``-q -f wheels`` and an abbreviated ``--find-l "
"wheels`` as ``--find-links wheels``. It stores a relative path given to a "
"pip option, such as ``--cert ca.pem`` or ``--find-links wheels``, as an "
"absolute path, and resolves a relative one already on file against the "
"environment's directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/metadata.rst:79
msgid ""
"Options naming a one-shot input or an output location (``-r``/``--"
"requirement``, ``--requirements-from-script``, ``--group``, ``--report``, "
"``--log``, ``--log-file``, ``--local-log``, ``--cache-dir``, ``-t``/``--"
"target``, ``--prefix``, ``--root`` and ``--src``) apply only to the command "
"they were given on, so pipx neither stores nor replays them. An abbreviation "
"the current pip finds ambiguous but an older pip reads as one of these, such "
"as ``--requirem`` before pip added ``--requirements-from-script``, counts as "
"that option, and one that could name a source option goes through the replay "
"check below. An abbreviation that could also name a flag, such as ``--b`` "
"for ``--break-system-packages``, takes no value, so the option after it is "
"read on its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/metadata.rst:88
msgid ""
"On POSIX, a replay stops with an error before the installer runs when a "
"stored ``-f``/``--find-links``, ``-c``/``--constraint``, ``--build-"
"constraint``, ``--cert``, ``--client-cert``, `uv <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/"
">`_'s ``--config-file``, ``--project``, ``--directory``, ``--overrides``/``--"
"override`` or ``--excludes``/``--exclude``, or ``file://`` or local-path "
"index URL names a path another account could change, because it or a "
"directory above it is writable by others or owned by another user. The "
"record stays as it is; passing the options again with ``--pip-args`` uses "
"them for that run. ``pipx list --outdated`` reports such an environment as "
"failed rather than checking it against that path."
msgstr ""

